# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Fling measures the sacrificed creature's power, while Perilous Myr deals two more damage when it dies.
# Forcing: Growth makes the smaller Myr four power; Fling plus its death trigger then deals six. Growing and throwing the Bear deals only five.
# AI behavior: Giant Spider blocks an attempted combat win. The opponent has no spells or abilities.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Growth makes Myr four power, Fling sacrifices it, and Fling plus Myr's death trigger deal six.
#   LOSE = Growth makes the Bear five power and Fling sacrifices it, leaving the opponent at one.
#   TIMEOUT = sacrifice selection, Fling's target, or Myr's death-trigger target did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Giant Growth — raises one creature's power, forcing a target choice.
#   Fling — converts that creature's power into direct damage by sacrificing it.
#   Perilous Myr — the smaller throw whose death adds two more damage.
#   Grizzly Bears — the tempting larger throw that falls one damage short.
#   Giant Spider — makes attacking an ineffective shortcut.
# Protocol path: Grow Myr, target the opponent with Fling, sacrifice Myr, then aim Myr's trigger at the opponent.
[metadata]
